 "patch": "vllm/0785-perf-worker-compact-packed-vocab-tables-and-expand-d.patch",
 "verdict": "corrected-meets-mark",
 "verdict_reason": "Both release-test failures were #998's and both are fixed by a narrow change (3 files, +20/-8). On the path serving takes at TP3 (TileLang head, carve-out on), the corrected patch saves 1,023.1 MiB of regular memory a rank (deterministic, both runs), moves draft-MoE slabs whose layers run 7.0-8.6% (layer 0) and 1.5-2.6% (layer 1) faster beyond the interval, and every vocab, head, markov and MoE output is bit-identical to the base. Caveats: the saving is 1,023 MiB, not the PR's 1,263 MiB, because on this base the lm_head's carve-out buffer already holds candidate-50 0763's screening table and has no slack (the PR's own script still reports 1,263 because it builds the 1107 layout); the startup floor and the prefill/decode core metrics need the screen at tp3-switched and were not measured here; the as-shipped candidate-53 cannot load the head at TP3 at all.",
 "base_of_patch": "candidate-53 series through 0784 (vllm tree c0e25ff1 minus 0785); corrected tree d0ecca479dfd24baadba2044db71754e9410f7e8",
 "host": "sp8 (spark-0016), one GB10",
 "image": "spark-ds41f:candidate-50 sha256:8c1ea1f62f62c3e2adc03b645c091a5499cf7163101aca32875c894b96f155db",
 "arms": {
  "base": "candidate-50 + candidate-50/no1009/overlay (4 files)",
  "c53": "candidate-50 + candidate-53 tree (c0e25ff1) versions of the 33 differing source files",
  "fix": "candidate-50 + corrected tree (d0ecca47) versions of the same 33 files"
 },
 "root_causes": [
  {
   "failure": "tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_vocab.py: Fatal Python error: Segmentation fault (exit 139/-11)",
   "test": "test_packed_bf16_lm_head_carveout_shares_single_buffer_with_screen_wq",
   "kernel": "build_screen_weights (vocab.py:2727, W_q[start:end] = (sign << 7) | u7), reached from PackedBf16LmHeadMethod.process_weights_after_loading -> _ensure_screen_weights",
   "cause": "Use after free, not an out-of-bounds read of the compacted tables. #998 was written on 1107, where the lm_head carve-out buffer held only the BF16 head. candidate-50's 0763 (certified two-pass lm_head vocab screen) allocates the TileLang head's carve-out buffer at n x 1.25k BF16 and sets layer._carveout_screen_wq, a view of the buffer's tail at [1.5nk, 2.5nk) bytes, for the 8-bit screening table. #998's display_carveout.compact(packed.values) copies only the packed rows into a new tight buffer and closes the old one (cuMemFree + cuDestroyExternalMemory), so the screening view dangles; build_screen_weights then writes into the freed range. Diagnostic (test shape n=16384, k=4096): before compact the view lies in the live 160 MiB buffer at 0x334e00000; after it the only buffer is a new 96 MiB one at 0xf5a010600000 and cuPointerGetAttribute on the view returns CUDA_ERROR_INVALID_VALUE (no mapping). The fixed tree keeps the 160 MiB buffer with the view inside it. A semantic conflict between #998 and 0763: no file conflict, so stacking found nothing.",
   "serving_impact": "Serving takes this path at every TP3 shape (tp3-triangle sets SPARK_DS41F_DISPLAY_CARVEOUT_WEIGHTS=1; tp3-switched and tp3-triangle-4k extend it; the recipe runs --linear-backend tilelang). At the TP3 shard shape (43,136 x 5,120) candidate-53 fails at the same write with 'CUDA error: invalid argument' (raw/bench-serving-c53-boot1.txt), so no TP3 rank of candidate-53 as built can load its head.",
   "fix": "packed_bf16.py: compact the head only when its buffer holds no screening table (getattr(layer, '_carveout_screen_wq', None) is None). With the table the buffer is exactly 2.5nk bytes (1.5nk packed + 1.0nk table), so there is no slack to reclaim and nothing is lost. display_carveout.compact() docstring states the caller must hold the only live view. The embedding table still compacts (432 -> 320 MiB at TP3); the b12x head path (no screening table) still compacts."
  },
  {
   "failure": "tests/kernels/quantization/test_deepseek_v41_expert_scale_codes.py::test_process_weights_replaces_w13_before_preparing_w2: AttributeError: '_Plan' object has no attribute 'max_rows' (tilelang.py:224)",
   "cause": "#998 made TileLangExperts.process_weights_after_loading read self._plan.max_rows and self._plan._has_mid_tiles() unconditionally, on every shape, to decide its carve-out move; the test's minimal _Plan stub implements only prepare_weight.",
   "decision": "Fix the code, not the test: the stub is not stale (it is the minimal contract of what weight preparation needs), the decode-only test serves only the carve-out move, and display_carveout.move() is a no-op without the carve-out. The test is now evaluated only when display_carveout.required(); without the carve-out (TP4, the switched TP4..TP8 shapes, the release tests) preparation is exactly the base's. MoeExpertsV41Plan always sets max_rows and _has_mid_tiles(), so the TP3 placement is unchanged (DSpark draft routers: max_rows = max_num_seqs x query_rows, decode-only; target routers: max_num_batched_tokens, mid tiles, not moved)."
  }
 ],
